2. TORQUE CEILING vs COLLECTIVE THRUST (the unidirectional f_i >= 0 constraint)
   Two rotors at f_lo, two at f_hi: T = 2(f_lo+f_hi), tau = lever*2(f_hi-f_lo),
   0 <= f_lo, f_hi <= f_max  =>  tau_max(T) = lever * min(T, 4 f_max - T).
   At hover collective T = m g this gives tau_max = lever * m g, INDEPENDENT of T/W;
   the global maximum lever*T_max/2 sits at half throttle (and needs a climb).
